1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,130
Listen to a talk in a history class.

2
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:08,290
Petra is an ancient city located in present-day Jordan.

3
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:15,260
It was established as early as 312 BC as the capital city of the Nabataean Kingdom.

4
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:18,170
The Nabataeans were skilled traders

5
00:00:18,170 --> 00:00:26,130
and Petra became a major trading hub because of its strategic location along caravan routes that linked the East and West.

6
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:32,256
Petra's architecture is unique because much of it was carved directly into the rose-red

7
00:00:32,256 --> 00:00:33,240
cliffs of the region.

8
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:37,505
The most famous structure in the city is known as the treasury,

9
00:00:37,505 --> 00:00:40,020
but it is actually a tomb.

10
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:43,230
The city also featured a complex system to manage water

11
00:00:43,230 --> 00:00:45,741
including dams, cisterns,

12
00:00:45,741 --> 00:00:50,020
and water channels that allowed it to thrive in the arid region.

13
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:55,846
These advanced water engineering structures were crucial for the survival of its inhabitants, given

14
00:00:55,846 --> 00:00:59,040
the low amount of moisture that was available naturally.

15
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:05,220
In addition to its architectural and engineering feats, Petra is significant for its cultural exchanges.

16
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:10,340
As a trading center, it facilitated the exchange of goods, ideas,

17
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,050
and customs between diverse peoples.

18
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:18,104
This blend of cultures is evident in the various architectural styles seen in the

19
00:01:18,104 --> 00:01:18,465
city,

20
00:01:18,465 --> 00:01:21,473
which include influences from Greek, Roman,

21
00:01:21,473 --> 00:01:24,040
and indigenous Nabataean designs.

22
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:29,180
Next, we will explore how archaeologists rediscovered Petra in the 19th century.
